WEBVTT

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.240
I wonder if Rin-san's will be okay.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:16.870
I'm honestly more shocked that the missing 
half of her body has already grown back...

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:21.250
Maybe that kind of damage 
was too much, even for her.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:25.500
She's all healed up, 
but she's still completely out of it.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.420
G-Grandfather...

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:42.110
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.010
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.270
<i>One week ago, the Zoble Empire 
was overthrown by a military coup d'état</i>

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:11.580
<i>organized by Imperial Army General Piscalat
 and Imperial Navy Admiral Neput.</i>

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.770
<i>Their new weapons allowed them to 
easily pierce the nation's defenses</i>

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:16.240
<i>and occupy the capital.</i>

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:20.320
<i>The bodies of Emperor Takeshita and 
Empress Brandy were both discovered,</i>

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:21.960
<i>and Prime Minister Biarov has since</i>

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:25.100
<i>announced his intent to work 
with the occupying military.</i>

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:30.710
<i>Thus the coup d'état was a success, 
giving rise to a reborn Zoble Empire.</i>

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:34.670
I suppose it's a rather 
happy ending on the surface, but...

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:36.750
In reality, we've got a mountain of headaches.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.680
I'm honestly not sure where to start.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:44.310
You've been going through documents for 
three days. Are you going to be all right?

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.390
Idaten don't really suffer the kind of 
deterioration you're worried about.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.260
You, meanwhile, seem to be on the ropes.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.440
Is sleep deprivation an issue for demons?

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:57.280
<b>#9 Shadows</b>

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:55.520
My body is fine, but I think my human 
brain is approaching its limit...

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.280
Barcode seems to be fine, though.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.690
His demonic powers have a 
strong influence on his brain.

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:04.510
I've finished my survey of all the bodies
 we've been able to confirm.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:09.120
Of those, thirteen demons and two babies
 remain unaccounted for.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.120
Kuraishi, Buzz, and Raki...

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.500
These three are Takeshita 
and Brandy's biological children.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.260
Then there's Miku, who fled 
after tricking the Demon Lord.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.010
Umeyo, inside of whom two 
demon children are gestating.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.790
Merku, Umeyo's assistant.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:27.850
Ferlandia, who's a skilled
 negotiator with humans

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.210
and has a degree of influence 
in the underworld.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:34.030
Meliano, who fled via an unauthorized flight.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:36.090
Kroft, who is skilled at subterranean travel.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.780
We've already confirmed
that he dug tunnels to escape.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.570
Lastly are the Super Beefy Bros., 
who are worthless.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:44.070
Those four were obliterated 
without a trace by Rin-san,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.160
so you can take them off the list.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.210
You have surveillance on your own allies?

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:51.370
You're every bit as thorough 
as the Demon Lord himself.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:52.960
Well, you know...

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.340
General Piscalat, of the escaped demons, 
do any strike you as a particular threat?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.620
Umeyo has the most combat prowess,

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.160
but I'd say Miku poses the greatest 
overall threat given the situation.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.060
I thought as much...

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.220
An incident came to 
my attention three days ago.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:10.350
It happened at the Frohz estate, home to 
a major noble family in the nation of Yakini.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:14.720
Bodies were found slaughtered in a way
that a human would've struggled to manage.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.380
Raki seems the likely culprit.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.530
The Frohz estate is a beautiful property, 
so I suspect she just waltzed in.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.360
She just... waltzed into a pretty house
 while on the run

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:27.200
and killed everyone who lives there?
 Is she a moron?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.790
The fact that she vanished afterward

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:34.770
suggests she's traveling 
with someone who took her away.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:38.340
Additionally, during the war, 
Neput killed a decoy of Kuraishi's.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:43.470
That felt a little too fragile. 
Must be a human decoy.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:49.110
It would suggest that my and Neput's betrayal
was already discovered by the time they fled.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.970
What is this Kuraishi like?

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.770
The simplest way to describe him...

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:55.400
is to say he's like you.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.220
So, you want use of this place for an 
indefinite amount of time. Is that right?

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:05.400
That's a tall order, 
even for you, Prince Kuraishi.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.020
Aw, don't be like that, Gibaccho!

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.920
We're brothers who hit it rich
in weapon smuggling

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.290
and human trafficking, aren't we?

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.340
Not sure I see a whole lot of reason
 to work with you

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.720
now that you don't have the 
empire backing you up.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:20.100
Organ harvesting, human experimentation,

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.670
anthrax cultivation, and bioweapons...

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:26.600
It's no Zoble, but the plethora
 of facilities and secrets here

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:30.300
makes it the perfect place to host 
the Demon Lord when he resurfaces.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.700
What the hell are you going on about?

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.680
Oh, right, right. You want 
a reason to work with me...

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.060
You can bet I've got that.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:42.940
See, if you shut up and do as I say, 
then you won't all have to die.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:48.090
He's used his influence as a prince 
of Zoble and his power as a demon

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:51.530
to establish a variety of connections 
in the human underworld.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:55.520
Miku's got no real resources, 
so when you consider Kuraishi's

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:59.040
potential havens and pawns to play, 
he's a pretty dangerous opponent.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.090
Hey, Miku, are we seriously 
going to stay here?

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.710
Couldn't we have stopped at an 
internet cafe that has a shower?

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:09.820
Sadly, there are no such cafes
 that don't check ID

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.200
or have security cameras.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.970
Are you willing to risk your 
life for a shower, Merku?

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.580
You say that, but you've been staring 
at social media for the past three days.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:19.940
What are you looking at?

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:23.110
The blog posts and comments 
of pathetic humans,

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.840
the times they were posted, 
and their leaked personal information.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:27.690
Their shopping histories, too.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:32.980
It's enough info for me to figure out
 exactly who these people are.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.580
First, I need to find the perfect prey...

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.960
Lastly, that nun has apparently woken up.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:43.950
She's definitely interesting 
as a research subject...

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:46.960
But for now, we'll just keep her in 
protective custody until things settle down.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.040
Unnershtood...

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.930
You should get some rest, too, General.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.220
Right...

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:58.590
G-General Piscalat?!

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:02.400
You awake? Then hand over the bed, please.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:05.800
If you're hungry, 
grab something out of the fridge.

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.230
You can throw on whatever 
clothes you can find, too.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.600
General Piscalat!

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:16.450
Y-You attacked our homeland, 
killing innocent people and kidnapping—

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:19.280
That's enough. Just let me get some sleep.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:24.050
Zoble's gone now, anyway. No more invasions.

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:26.090
What more do you want?

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:32.590
Apologies? Reparations? Take it up with 
Biarov when the reconstruction is finished.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:36.620
I'd like to help 
with the reconstruction, then.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.740
I'll do whatever I can!

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:41.530
Can you drive a 18-wheeler?

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:42.480
Excuse me?

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.860
Do you have enough stamina 
to clear rubble all day?

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.490
Enough medical knowledge
to treat the injured?

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:54.920
Have you ever prepared food
 to serve thousands efficiently?

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:58.240
Almost everyone in this country
 has military training.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:01.370
You're just a "good person" 
who doesn't know how to do much

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.650
other than pray for people.

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:05.830
Which means you're essentially useless.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:12.080
If you want to be helpful, then shut up and 
let me sleep so I can get back to work.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:16.730
That'll accomplish more than if 
you literally worked yourself to death.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.190
<i>I can't argue.</i>

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:24.270
<i>I've been reminded of how 
powerless I am so many times...</i>

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:27.180
I want power.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.600
The kind of power I need to protect people.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:31.930
The thing is, Gill-san,

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:35.660
the training that Idaten go through 
to get strong is super painful.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.410
That's fine. I'll endure whatever it takes.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:41.960
You sound kind of like Hayato, Gill-san.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.670
I wonder if the person who pulls you out 
has an influence on your personality...

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:50.250
<i>Drawing out an Idaten involves adding your 
own thoughts to a nascent existence</i>

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.280
<i>in order to shorten the amount of time
 required for manifestation.</i>

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.670
<i>As a result, the personality of the drawer</i>

00:08:55.670 --> 00:08:58.890
<i>has a certain degree of influence 
in shaping the Idaten drawn.</i>

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:03.220
<i>The desire of the nun, who was rocked 
to the core by how powerless she felt,</i>

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:05.290
<i>mixed with Hayato's own desire</i>

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:08.900
<i>to create an Idaten who thirsted for strength
 that would allow her to defend others.</i>

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.150
The thing is...

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:14.540
Hey, you stupid old bitch. 
How long are you gonna just sit there?

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.420
Let's get training! Now!

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.110
Damn it, Granny!

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:24.330
Screw you, then! Like I give a shit!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.160
You can rot up there for all I care!

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.670
<i>After learning the Demon Lord's identity,</i>

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:31.420
<i>Rin-san seems to have lost her will to live.</i>

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:34.380
<i>Here's hoping that doesn't 
have a negative outcome.</i>

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:40.330
Pete-kun, I've found the emperor's 
administrative password,

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.560
so could you pull up his files 
and organize them for me?

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.990
Huh?! O-Oh, right away!

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:46.230
Pass everything you find 
along to General Piscalat.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:50.480
How is he able to figure out 
passwords just by sitting there?

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:54.230
How's it going, Prontea-san? 
Have you found any clues?

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:56.490
I've been poking around as best I can,

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:59.290
but to be honest, I haven't 
found anything interesting.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.990
Nothing like the Demon Lord's research data?

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:04.200
There's a major hitch with that...

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.630
It won't display on a monitor 
and can't be printed out.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:11.360
It's some sort of file format that can 
only be observed by those

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.690
who link their consciousnesses to the computer.

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:17.470
And I have no idea what it actually says.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.990
<i>Prontea's intellect and 
academic accomplishments</i>

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:23.130
<i>are on par with an average adult male.</i>

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:25.790
<i>When confronted with 
professorial-level research data,</i>

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:28.600
<i>it appears little more than an 
incomprehensible collection of symbols.</i>

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:35.280
So I tried writing it out to show 
someone like you or Professor Gachikama...

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.610
But diving in and out of cyber-consciousness 
while jotting a bunch of technobabble

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:41.060
you don't understand is a real pain!

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:43.320
It took me four hours to get this little bit.

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:48.200
Humans... demons... 
and human-demon hybrids...

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.750
It appears to be three 
patterns of genetic code.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.140
Is that of any help?

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:54.820
Since I've got access
 to Gyudo and Nickel's bodies,

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.690
I would've learned it sooner or later.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:11:00.380
See what I mean? A total waste of four hours!

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.820
And there are tens of thousands 
of files like this.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:06.100
I'm sorry, but you'll have to give up
 on the Demon Lord's research.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.810
If you're dead set on getting access to it,

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:11.350
we'll either need to invent a monitor 
that can display brain imagery...

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:15.670
Or you'll have to train until you 
can use this kind of ability.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.660
You could always study until 
you understand what you're—

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:19.740
Nope!

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:25.000
I think any more would be a waste of time.
 I'm going to do something else.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.740
Any suggestions?

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.720
We've been able to identify 
the nine demons who escaped.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:32.610
As soon as we confirm their locations, 
go ahead and eliminate them.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:37.500
And in the meantime, I'd like you 
to help train the other Idaten.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:41.100
Go ahead and make them strong enough 
to defeat the powerful demons

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.510
on the scale of Brandy and Nickel.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.760
Anything less won't be of much use.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.270
That's a pretty big ask.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:51.690
Are we really going to need that 
kind of firepower in the future?

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:55.440
If the demons are able to continue 
evading us for long enough...

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.690
I get the feeling we will.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:02.710
She looks good.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:08.990
<b>Buzz & Meliano</b>

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:08.430
More... More!

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:16.750
<b>Hotel District 
Raki & Kroft</b>

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:16.030
Hey, Kroft, I'm hungry.

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:16.750
Right, right.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:20.510
Could you throw together twelve servings' 
worth of food and bring it up?

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.760
We're out of money...

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.340
Raki, could you grab some more?

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:27.720
Here.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:31.830
<i>Raki's power is essentially 
the same as Brandy's.</i>

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.860
<i>She can extend her hair
 up to several kilometers,</i>

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:35.460
<i>so thin as to be invisible...</i>

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:38.150
<i>The difference is her 
lack of strength when doing it.</i>

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:43.680
<i>But it's great at stealing money 
from people without making a scene.</i>

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.910
<i>It's one reason I haven't ditched this idiot.</i>

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:50.100
<i>I'm going to need her power on the run.</i>

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:52.650
<i>That's become clear to me 
during this time.</i>

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:55.190
Room service!

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:56.880
Ah, it's here.

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:59.130
Kroft, something's wrong!

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:03.090
The person delivering room service... 
He doesn't weigh anything!

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:08.510
Excuse me, sir? 
I brought the food you ordered...

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:11.520
Sir?

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:18.500
Strange. How'd they figure it out?

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.910
The place is surrounded.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:23.200
There was no sign of anyone 
suspicious escaping.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.400
They have to be hiding somewhere.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.920
I don't see them anywhere.

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:32.910
In that case...

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:34.250
Underground!

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:37.370
One of the escaped demons is 
supposedly good at subterranean travel!

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.380
Bingo!

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:43.090
They've barely got a minute's head start. 
Should be easy enough to catch up.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.970
Huh... that's a lot of branches.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.970
I hope you don't think that'll 
be enough to get away.

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:53.190
Prontea-san!

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.180
<i>I don't think he's going to find them...</i>

00:13:56.310 --> 00:14:03.340
<b>Lots of branches</b>

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:58.750
<i>All you have to do to 
severely complicate a search</i>

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:04.480
<i>is create a bunch of dummy routes 
while covering up the real one.</i>

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:04.500
<b>Correct route</b>

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:04.500
<b>Buried</b>

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.250
I couldn't find them...

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:07.780
I figured as much.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:11.690
<i>Damn... Why didn't I account for a 
subterranean escape in the first place?</i>

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.700
<i>We'll probably never get 
another chance like this.</i>

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:16.950
That was a close one!

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:19.170
But what's going on? How'd they find us?!

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.660
We used an alias when we checked in.
 They must have looked into it.

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:26.730
We may never be safe 
entering a human town again.

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.650
Oh, no!

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:32.470
Does that mean we have to stay underground?

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:37.180
Without any beds or baths? No way!

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:44.410
<i>Things are too dangerous to spend long 
listening to this moron's bullshit...</i>

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:47.240
<i>But that doesn't change the fact
 that I need her power.</i>

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:49.570
Kroft...

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:53.200
I don't want you to die, Raki.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:56.730
I'll try to comfort you 
through the painful parts...

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.710
So please, listen to me.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.640
O-Okay...

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:02.960
<i>Damn it. I hate to do this, 
but there's no other way.</i>

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:08.600
<i>I guess I'll love you.</i>

